md rewrites the two bullets as hyphens, so a command asked to remove
the paragraph at the bottom also edits the list in the middle.

RemoveCommand rebuilds the whole document with BlockFormatter, which
prints every unordered item with a hyphen and has no memory of the
marker the source used. A block the user did not name must come
through byte for byte. Splicing the removal out of the source, as
insert-before already does for its insert, would fix this.
